discussion_comments.comment_body:
**should-fix (small):** Two notes on this block.

1. The bare `catch {}` now hides a leftover `${path}.tmp-<uuid>` without leaving any trace. I ran a probe with your spy setup, and `Worker.md.tmp-<uuid>` stays in the artifacts dir after the throw. `agent://` discovery skips it because it only matches `*.md` (`agent-protocol.ts:397`), so it's harmless there, but nothing records that it exists. Sibling code in `utils/atomic-file.ts:155` logs this case with `logger.warn(...)`. A one-liner would match that:
```ts
await fs.rm(tempPath, { force: true }).catch(cleanupError => {
	logger.warn("Failed to remove staged artifact", { tempPath, error: toError(cleanupError).message });
});
```
2. The PR's motivating case is Windows `EBUSY`. `removeWithRetries` from `@oh-my-pi/pi-utils` (`packages/utils/src/temp.ts:96`) already retries `EBUSY`/`EPERM` on win32. Using it here, wrapped the same way, would usually remove the temp file as well as keep the original error. Optional, your call.

